<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--Recycler Trees get their own file due to the giant usage cases and guidelines. They are still Conduit Trees.
  Guide for T1 recycling tree:
    -This tree cannot break down steel.
    -Return on materials is 1/4th of the ingredients, rounded to nearest whole.
    -Normal components always add 1 shocksap
    -Advanced components add 3 shocksap
    -Add +3 steel for every components used
    -Cannot convert structures
    -Armor produces Endosap instead of shocksap
  
  -->



  <!--Reclaimer Tree: recycles manufactured items into usable materials-->

  <ThingDef ParentName="TreeBase">
    <defName>ET_RecycleTreeTierOne</defName>
    <label>Primwood Reclaimer Tree</label>
    <description>The Primwood Reclaimer tree is one of the Conduit trees that Terratech devotees learn to properly nurture, enabling tribes to live safely under natural resources. The roots of a reclaimer tree 'captures' any nearby items within a small radius, breaking them down into natural, usable materials that may be useful to Terratech colonies.
This particular tree is capable of breaking down basic industrial items. As this is only the first generation tree, the amount of returned items is rather low, and it is incapable of breaking down steel. Still, it gives a use for any manufactured guns or mechanoid remains that may pop up. 

The process always breaks materials down to their most fundamental components, resulting in a 25-30% yield. Further generations of this tree will be able to process more complex items, and output more useful resources.</description>
